{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.Su2CharactersAndQuantumDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.Su2CharactersAndQuantumDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Character_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Character_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The trivial representation has character `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Character_fundamental","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Character_fundamental","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.lean#L58-L62","doc":"**The fundamental representation: `dim_q(V_1) = q + q⁻¹ = [2]_q`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Character_mul_q_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Character_mul_q_sub","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.lean#L40-L56","doc":"**Multiplied by `q − q⁻¹`, the character at `q` is `q^{n+1} − q^{−(n+1)}`**: the\ncharacter is the symmetric quantum integer `[n+1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Character_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Character_one","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.lean#L36-L38","doc":"**At `x = 1` the character is the dimension `n + 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2Character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2Character","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.lean#L32-L34","doc":"The character of `V_n` at `x`, written as `x⁻ⁿ · Σ_{i=0}^{n} x^{2i}`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension","label":"ex:su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/su2-characters-and-quantum-dimension.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}